# An extension's popup shows when its button is clicked. Chrome makes it as a child of the profile's
# hidden window, and shows it only while that window is on screen: with the window ordered out (one
# way to stop its compositor ticking at idle) every popup stayed hidden while the scenarios that
# click a button, which check what the popup does, still passed.
budget rss=600 stalls50=5
cra://debug?installExtension=${FIXTURES}/Extension
relaunch
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=ext
wait 3
cra://debug?extensionAction=${EXTENSION_ID}
wait 2
expect-log extension popup shown
cra://dismiss
cra://debug?removeExtension=${EXTENSION_ID}
